    notes: "The cookie lasts 400 days, the longest browsers keep one, rather than 20 years, and it's named `__Host-session_token` over HTTPS so no other site on the domain can set it. It's sent again every time the app loads and asks who's signed in, rather than with the hourly refresh, which a room's socket may be the one to make. The Workspace stores an HMAC of the cookie's token, keyed by `SESSION_SECRET`, rather than the token, so its database holds no live sessions and changing the secret signs everyone out, as changing ember-rust's secret key base does. When another tab signs the browser in as someone else, a tab whose room then answers as them switches to that person rather than sending as them under the old name. Resetting a password, or removing or banning the person, ends all of their sessions (`accounts.reset-password`, `accounts.remove-person`, `accounts.ban`), and a new password from the profile ends all but the one that saves it (`users.profile`), where ember-rust's leaves them signed in. A session unused for 400 days, as long as its cookie lasts, is refused, where ember-rust's last forever, so a token kept from a browser that's long gone stops working too.",
