    sources: [],
    notes: "This port's own, beside `bots.slack-webhook`. A message keeps its cards as JSON in `messages.cards` (room migration 0034), as a file message keeps its file, rather than in its body as Action Text attachments, which the rich text pipeline would sanitize as markup, the editor would drop as an administrator edits, and outgoing webhooks would hand to bots. A card's text is rich text in the stored form, kept by `prepareBody` and drawn through `displayBody`. The warning color is Slack's own, `#daa038`, since ember-rust's only orange, Campfire's `--lch-orange`, is too near the negative red for a bar to tell them apart. Images load from the sender's host, as link previews' do: as they near the screen, and without a referrer. Block Kit's parts keep Slack's layout but not all its names: a card block is a small card (`tiles`), so it isn't taken for a whole card, and a section keeps its accessory beside its text. A video can't play here, so it links to its page. Markdown is read with marked 18.1.0, in the Worker only, and a table's cells, as Slack's, take no header row.",
